homelab-block-link (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=high

  * SECURITY (post-cutover #69): the link page works only for a visitor
    signed in as the account the message was delivered to. Until now a
    link covering ONE account kept a one-click block for whoever held it
    ("the token is the credential"), and the footer that carries the link
    is quoted into every reply and forward: since #67 the original sender
    routinely held a working link and could block the alias they were
    writing to. Visibility.pm now has two modes, owner and guest; guest
    sees and may block nothing.
  * GET /l/:token with nobody signed in redirects to /login (and back to
    the link) BEFORE the link is looked up, so an anonymous visitor learns
    nothing, not even whether the link is valid. A session whose token no
    longer introspects gets the page with a Sign in button instead, so a
    sign-in that comes back unverifiable can never loop.
  * POST /l/:token takes the same guards as unblock, in the same order:
    the page's CSRF token (X-CSRF-Token, from the form's data-csrf), then a
    live sign-in, then the link, then that the visitor is one of its
    accounts. Signed in as another account: 403 "for another account".
  * Tests (visibility, chrome, signin, basic), README and the example
    config follow the new rule.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:30:00 -0600

homelab-block-link (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Unblock from the list: signed in, each row of the block list has an x.
    It asks first, in the shared theme's modal ("Unblock this address?",
    Cancel / Unblock), and the result shows as a toast. The browser's own
    confirm box asks if the theme's script did not load.
  * New POST /l/:token/unblock {address}. It calls the api endpoint that
    myaccount's Unblock button calls, with the visitor's own token, and
    domain-admin can only delete that account's own rows. It needs a CSRF
    token from the page (X-CSRF-Token, checked before anything else), a
    sign-in as one of the link's accounts, and the address on that
    account's block list as just read, so an allow entry is never removed
    here. An address already gone answers 404 with "gone".
  * Unblocking one of this message's own addresses brings its row in the
    add section back, ticked. Every address the visitor may block now has
    a row there; already-blocked ones are hidden and left out of the form.
  * An empty list says "Your block list is empty." (it may have just been
    emptied, not never filled).

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 19:05:00 -0600

homelab-block-link (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: a link that covers more than one account no longer shows anyone
    the other accounts' addresses or lets them block those. One message
    to two mailmasker users gets ONE link (the milter cannot vary it per
    recipient), and the page used to list every address on it, all
    checked: each recipient saw the other's address, even a Bcc'd one,
    and one Save blocked the other person's address on their account.
    Who sees and may block what is now one rule (Visibility.pm) used by
    both the page and the POST, which refuses anything the page would
    not offer.
  * An account's main address is never offered for blocking (it would
    stop all of that account's mail); domain-admin's self-service
    endpoint already refused it, the link's on-behalf path never did.
  * Optional sign-in through homelab-sso (sso: + session: in the config;
    see install-orchestrators/block-link-sso-provision.sh). Signed in as
    the link's account, the page shows that account's whole block list,
    read with the visitor's own token from the api myaccount uses:
    alphabetical ignoring case, one button cycling A to Z, Z to A, by
    domain A to Z and by domain Z to A, and a live filter that takes a
    Perl-style regular expression from the third character.
  * The button says "Add to Block List". Once it succeeds, the add
    section goes away and the addresses join the list. On a later visit
    only addresses not blocked yet are offered.
  * Manage Account buttons above and below the list, to myaccount's
    Mail section (block_link.manage_account_url).
  * Without an sso: block the app starts as before and the page is
    link-only (no Sign in, no list); the cross-account fix still
    applies. An old config keeps working unchanged.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 14:23:08 -0600

homelab-block-link (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The public pages at blockemail.<domain> (the "manage blocked addresses"
    form a link in a delivered email opens, and its "invalid link" and
    "link expired" pages) now have the same look as the rest of
    mailmasker: the shared top bar, footer and stylesheet from
    homelab-webtheme. They are templates now (templates/) instead of HTML
    built inside the controller. Same form, same fields, same Save call.
  * Save no longer sits at "Saving..." forever when the server cannot be
    reached, and the button is disabled while a save is in flight.
  * GET / redirects to https://mailmasker.org/ (web_theme.home_url), so
    the logo in the top bar leads somewhere instead of to a 404.
  * Depends on homelab-webtheme.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 10:01:16 -0600

